## Addendum 2026-09-07 (E-27, session 3 dce0b6e2, during the Lamentations OW-6 final check) — EVIDENCE-KIND CONFLATION: a tool decided what a file WAS from where it sat

A tool inferred a file's KIND from its directory and extension. Both describe where the runtime chose to put a file, not what the file is. The session
`tasks/` directory holds BOTH a subagent's complete JSONL reasoning transcript AND the captured stdout of a background shell command the ORCHESTRATOR
ran, under the same `<id>.output` name. `_transcript_manifest.py` enumerated it with a bare `glob("*.output")` and recorded every non-empty file as an
"unmapped transcript"; `_mirror_transcripts.py` copied every one into the durable transcript store. Four claude-fable-5-1 stage-1 auditors were then
launched against 29 files described to them as subagent transcripts. Only 11 were. The other 18 were orchestrator shell output: validator dumps, a
corpus jsonl excerpt, a directory listing, and this ledger's own markdown.

WHY IT IS A CLASS: it fails silently and it fails toward false assurance. The auditors would have returned coverage digits counting 29 transcripts and
~11 MB with findings about orchestrator commands rather than subagent behaviour, and the OW-6 close gate would have passed them, because the gate
asserted that a coverage statement was PRESENT and never that it was TRUE. The digits would have looked complete.

CONTROL: `is_subagent_transcript()` reads ONE line and requires a JSON object carrying `agentId` or `isSidechain`. Content-based on purpose — the
runtime's id prefixes happen to sort a/b today, that is an undocumented convention, and a manifest silently depending on it would break without saying
so. Every tool that enumerates a task directory applies it and REPORTS what it excluded. The 23 shell outputs were MOVED (never deleted) to
`sp_durable/shell_outputs/<session>/`, each sha256-verified at the destination before its source was unlinked. Regression test
`_test_transcript_discriminator.py`: 13 synthetic vectors plus every real file on both sides of the quarantine boundary; GREEN.

DETECTION HONESTY: found while chasing an unrelated missing path, not by a guard designed to catch it. Severity is scored on counterfactual blast
radius, not on the small observed impact — the auditors were stopped about ten minutes in and no deliverable from that wave was written or used.
The fault is the orchestrator's, not the agents': they were given a defective assignment. Both waves are recorded in the lane's attempt receipts.

## Addendum 2026-09-07 (E-28, same session) — EVIDENCE DECAY, AND THE UNFALSIFIABLE COVERAGE CLAIM

Two joined facts, both observed rather than theorised.

(a) The runtime DELETES subagent transcripts while the session is still running. One transcript recorded in the Lamentations manifest with a size and a
sha256 was gone hours later and had never been mirrored: its content no longer exists anywhere. Two others survived only because the mirror had already
copied them. A fourth vanished between a mirror `--dry-run` and the real run seconds apart. An earlier orchestrator conclusion that absent transcripts
had "NEVER been written, not truncated" was true of the attempts then sampled and wrong as a general claim; it is corrected here rather than quietly
replaced.

(b) A coverage statement that nothing can contradict is not evidence. The OW-6 gate checked that each auditor SAID what it covered. Nothing compared the
saying to the slice plan or to the manifest.

CONTROL: `_mirror_transcripts.py` runs at every wave landing and BEFORE any final check is launched; audit slices resolve each transcript to the durable
mirror first and fall back to the live directory only if the mirror lacks it; a transcript held in neither is dropped from the slice and REPORTED as
permanently lost, never silently omitted. `_final_check_reconcile.py` compares every stage-1 packet against the slice plan and the manifest — assigned
vs reported transcripts, disjointness between slices, union against the manifest, and the byte arithmetic a mechanical pass claiming 100% must satisfy —
and the close gate refuses on RED. The stage-2 checker must state transcript coverage explicitly and the gate asserts that it did.

RESIDUAL RISK, STATED: the mirror runs when the orchestrator runs it, so a transcript written and deleted between two mirror runs is lost leaving only
its manifest digest. The window is narrowed, not closed.

BEARING ON OW-6c: the end-of-campaign re-check is bounded by what the durable store holds at that time, and books closed before the mirror existed have
no transcripts at all. The owner needs that when scoping the re-check, so the OW-6c decision packet must state it rather than imply a completeness that
is already gone.


