  a reason to narrow a review, drop a lane, shorten a wave, or prefer a weaker model. OW-15's check-in remains; the
  anxiety around it does not.
- **TOKEN EFFICIENCY WHERE WE CAN.** Efficiency means not WASTING effort, not spending less on the work itself:
  - pilot a wave before committing every execution in it, because a pipeline defect found on two agents is 42 agents
    of work not thrown away (this is what caught the packet-schema defect on 2026-09-15);
  - check a brief's schema against its landing validator BEFORE launching, not after (L-0018);
  - measure example wording before a brief offers it (L-0012);
  - re-run a tool rather than re-deriving its output by hand;
  - never re-run completed work merely because a session cleared (the receipt-gated idempotency law).
  None of these reduce the quality of a book; all of them reduce the tokens spent getting there.
- **WHAT THIS DOES NOT CHANGE.** Every substantive quality gate stands: the hard close gates, the OW-6 Fable final
  check, the OW-6b hard-book arms, dual-blind primaries with full coverage and no sampling, the distinct-checker
  separation, OW-7 capture, OW-10 cure binding and OW-13 model roles. This directive raises quality's priority; it
