### OW-17 AMENDMENT (a) (owner directive, 2026-09-15) - THE CROSS-GENERATION STANDING METHOD

Owner words (verbatim): "a directive for this but also other version we do this for. so it needs to be in teh standing methods that keep improving on hwo to chunk th bible. that future chiunkers will do. liek m7,8,9 and that methos and thing we learn liek this keep getting updated so the nexxt tiem we chunk we get better at all this."

OW-17 as first recorded creates ONE artefact: a per-book record for scholars. This amendment adds a SECOND, which is
different in reader, scope and lifetime, and is the one that compounds.

- **TWO DOCUMENTS, TWO READERS.**
  - PER BOOK, for a scholar: why these boundaries, what was contested, how it was settled, what is still open.
  - ACROSS GENERATIONS, for the next chunker: how to chunk the Bible well, and what each generation learned that
    changed the method. M7, M8, M9 and after.
- **THE SECOND IS NOT A LOG, IT IS A METHOD.** A learning log records what happened to us. The method record states
  what a later chunker should DO, and carries the reason and the evidence behind each rule so a successor can judge it
  rather than inherit it blindly. Every rule in it names the generation and the book that produced it.
- **IT VERSIONS AND IS HANDED FORWARD.** Each generation reads the previous version as a REQUIRED Phase-0 input,
  improves it from its own experience, and publishes the next version at its campaign close. A generation that ends
  without having updated it has not closed.
- **UPDATED AT EVERY BOOK CLOSE, NOT ONLY AT CAMPAIGN CLOSE.** A method improvement discovered in book 26 must be
  available to book 27 of the same campaign, not only to the next campaign. This is what turns 66 books into 66
  opportunities to get better instead of 66 repetitions.
- **IT CARRIES THE OPEN QUESTIONS IT COULD NOT SETTLE.** The most valuable thing one generation hands the next is the
  list of questions it could not answer with the witnesses it had, stated precisely enough to be worked on. An open
  question handed forward is worth more than a confident rule that was never tested.
- **SAME THREE GATES.** Pre-flight: the current version is read before a wave is designed, and a wave that contradicts
  it must say so deliberately. Mid-flight: a method change discovered in flight is captured when it is found, not
  reconstructed later. Post-flight: a Fable execution checks that what the book learned actually reached the method
  record, and that nothing in it is asserted without the evidence to support it.
- **WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN THE PER-BOOK RECORD.** The per-book record makes one book auditable. The method record
  makes every future book better. If only one survives, it should be this one.


### OW-17 AMENDMENT (b) (owner directive, 2026-09-15) - THE DIFFICULTY / RISK / BLAST-RADIUS ATLAS, AND CROSS-PASSAGE SOLUTION COMPARISON

Owner words (verbatim): "yes this will also help us map the bible what is hard, hardest, riskies, had a huge dependancys or blast radius, and over the compounding effects of doing this we can eve compar solutions and solitions across hard bble passage that migt be close in their fix or suuse or related"

This is the amendment that makes the method record COMPOUND instead of merely accumulate. The per-book record makes one
book auditable; the method record makes the next book better; the atlas makes the whole Bible navigable by where the
difficulty actually is.

- **THE ATLAS.** A map of the corpus by passage, carrying, per passage: how HARD it was, how RISKY, and how far its
  DEPENDENCIES reach. Built from the same landed review packets as everything else, so it costs almost nothing once the
  generator exists and cannot drift from what the reviewers said.
- **BLAST RADIUS IS THE SHARPEST AXIS, and it is not the same as difficulty.** A gloss error in one unit has radius one.
  A CONVENTION - which direction a received paragraph mark points, whether an apparatus read-form may be rendered,
  whether an in-span mark must be disclosed - has radius measured in books. Ranking by blast radius tells a future
  chunker WHAT TO DECIDE FIRST and WHERE TO SPEND A SECOND OPINION, which is a scheduling and assurance-allocation
  decision that M8 made by instinct and should have made from data.
- **DEPENDENCY CLASSES worth carrying**, each observed in Ezekiel: a shared frame whose decision governs every
  sub-unit inside it; a census or count claim that many units rest on; a convention that applies book-wide or
  campaign-wide; membership of a numbering-divergence zone; a seam shared between two adjacent units, where each is the
  other's far face.
- **CROSS-PASSAGE LINKAGE, AND IT IS ALREADY HAPPENING UNPROMPTED.** Reviewers spontaneously recognise structural
  recurrence and write it into their uncertainty fields - one M8 reviewer, deciding a seam, recorded that another
  cluster's disputed seam was "the same shape" and said so for whoever held it. That is exactly the linkage this
  amendment wants, and it is currently buried in free text. HARVEST it and make it first class rather than re-deriving
  it later.
- **COMPARE THE SOLUTIONS, NOT ONLY THE PROBLEMS.** Once two passages are linked as related, their treatments become
  comparable, and two outcomes matter:
  - they were treated the SAME - that is precedent, and a later passage of the same shape should cite it;
  - they were treated DIFFERENTLY - that is either a real distinction worth stating or an inconsistency worth fixing,
    and either way it must be surfaced rather than left to coincidence.
  Across 66 books this is how a corpus becomes internally consistent instead of merely locally defensible.
- **IT SPANS BOOKS AND GENERATIONS.** A hard passage in a later book should be able to find the already-solved passages
  it resembles, whichever book or generation solved them. The atlas therefore lives with the cross-generation method
  record, not inside one book.
- **SAME THREE GATES.** Pre-flight: the atlas is consulted when a wave is designed, so the highest-blast-radius
  questions are scheduled first and reviewed hardest. Mid-flight: linkages and radius estimates are captured as
  reviewers produce them. Post-flight: a checking execution verifies that every high-blast-radius question is in the
  atlas and that no linkage asserts a similarity no packet supports.
- **HONEST LIMIT.** Hardness and risk are partly judgements. The atlas records the MEASURED components separately from
  the judged ones and never presents a judgement as a measurement.


### OW-17 AMENDMENT (c) (owner directive, 2026-09-15) - THE METHOD-CHANGE PROPOSAL LOOP, ONE PROPOSER PER BOOK

Owner words (verbatim): "have a sub agent launch once every book to make proposed changes to thhow standing isntructions and log them so after we compelt a chunk all those poposed instructins chan ges are there too. and we can decide if they wer enessasary of jsut low reward. make that part of the standing instruction too"

- **ONE SUBAGENT PER BOOK** proposes changes to the standing method record, from that book's own evidence.
- **PROPOSALS ARE LOGGED, NOT APPLIED.** The proposer never edits the record. Proposals accumulate in
  `method_change_proposals.jsonl` so that at a book close every proposed instruction change is sitting there, together,
  and can be weighed as a set rather than absorbed one at a time.
- **EACH IS THEN ADJUDICATED** by a checking execution that is neither the proposer nor the orchestrator that ran the
  book: ADOPT / REJECT / DEFER, plus an independent rating of **NECESSARY / USEFUL / LOW-REWARD** with reasons. A
  proposal can be correct and still low-reward.
- **REJECTED AND DEFERRED PROPOSALS ARE KEPT WITH THEIR REASONS.** A rejected proposal is evidence: it stops the next
  generation re-proposing it blind, and it is half the data needed to judge the loop itself.
- **THE LOG MEASURES OUR OWN RULE-MAKING.** Adopt rate and low-reward rate, tracked across books, are the first data
  this campaign will have on whether its governance growth is earning its cost - the question OW-17's own §12 raises
  and which M8 could not answer. A mostly-low-reward log means narrow the loop; a mostly-necessary log means it should
  run more often than once a book.
- **WHY PROPOSING AND ADOPTING ARE SEPARATED.** Both failure modes were live in M8: a method that ossifies because
  nobody is tasked with improving it, and a method that bloats because any defect can become a rule. One role cannot
  guard against both.
- **BINDING FROM EZEKIEL ON**, and it is close-gate item 23: a book does not close with unadjudicated proposals.


## OW-18 (owner directive, 2026-09-15) - NO HALF-TRUTH AND NO IMPLICATION: EVERY CLAIM CARRIES ITS TRUE EVIDENCE TIER

Owner words (verbatim): "always do this (when true): I'll record that provenance honestly rather than imply I extracted it from a transcript. for instances likw that. it shoudlnt ever be implied when somethign is not ture. half truth of implication of something not ture is almsot jsut ass bad. especiualy with the bible. i think biblically half truth is a herrsey"

Occasion: two consecutive primary executions (`ezek_pr_OL_c15_a1#e1`, `ezek_pr_LF_c14_a1#e1`) completed with a
0-byte harness transcript, so their OW-7 Layer A records could not be EXTRACTED from a durable artifact the way the
28 landings before them were; they were TRANSCRIBED from the completion notification in the orchestrator's own
context. The orchestrator labelled the weaker tier in the record instead of letting the record read like the others.
The owner made that labelling a standing law rather than a one-time courtesy.

- **IMPLICATION IS ASSERTION.** A record that is silent about a change in how it was produced asserts, by its
  identical shape, that nothing changed. The standard is not "did I write a false sentence" but "would a careful
  reader draw a false conclusion from what I wrote and omitted". Where the answer is yes, the record is false. A
  half-truth is not a lesser error than a false statement; it is scored and escalated as one.
- **THE TIER TRAVELS WITH THE CLAIM.** Every substantive claim in every record names how it is known, using one of
  these words, and never a stronger one than is true:
  - **MEASURED** - produced this session by a tool whose output is in evidence (a digest, a count, a validator run).
  - **EXTRACTED** - read programmatically out of a durable artifact that still exists and can be re-read.
  - **TRANSCRIBED** - copied by hand or by eye from something that is NOT durably on disk (context, a notification,
    a screen). Weaker than EXTRACTED, because it cannot be re-derived after the session ends.
  - **REPORTED** - an agent's or a source's own claim about itself, carried forward but not independently checked.
  - **INFERRED** - derived by reasoning from claims of a named tier.
  - **ASSUMED** - a working assumption required to proceed, with no evidence behind it.
  - **UNAVAILABLE / UNKNOWN** - the evidence does not exist or could not be obtained. This is a VALUE, never a blank
    and never quietly replaced by the next-best thing (OW-7 already says this; OW-18 generalises it).
- **THE POSITIVE OBLIGATION, NOT JUST THE PROHIBITION.** When the normal evidence path fails, the record says which
  path was actually used, why the normal one was unavailable, what corroboration was obtained instead, and that the
  substitute is a weaker tier. Naming the corroboration does not upgrade the tier: the OL c15 and LF c14 records
  each carry a MEASURED deliverable digest that matches the TRANSCRIBED one, and they remain TRANSCRIBED records.
- **STRUCTURAL ENFORCEMENT, NOT MEMORY.** Silence must be made impossible rather than discouraged. Record schemas
  carry an explicit carrier/tier field, and the landing and receipt tools REFUSE a record that omits it. An
  orchestrator who forgets OW-18 is stopped by the tool; a tool that cannot represent the weaker tier is the defect,
  and is fixed rather than worked around.
- **IT BINDS THE SCHOLAR-FACING RECORD MOST OF ALL.** In the OW-17 record, the atlas and anything published, a
  boundary's warrant carries its tier: a seam corroborated by a Masoretic mark that was MEASURED in the inventory is
  not written the same way as a seam resting on a reviewer's REPORTED reading. A reader who cannot tell measurement
  from assertion cannot check us, and unfalsifiable authority over the text of scripture is precisely what this
  project exists to avoid. The owner's ground for this is theological as well as methodological, and is recorded as
  such in his own words above.
- **IT BINDS AGENTS, NOT ONLY THE ORCHESTRATOR.** Reviewer briefs already require a `checks_not_run` /
  `not_verified` field; OW-18 makes the omission of one a form problem rather than a style note, and extends the
  duty to any field where a reviewer could imply a check it did not run.
- **RELATION TO EXISTING POLICY.** The owner's global operating policy already separates Confirmed / Inferred /
  Assumed / Unknown and forbids silently promoting an assumption. OW-18 does not replace it: it closes the gap that
  policy leaves open, which is provenance DEGRADATION passing unmarked because the output still looks the same. It
  lowers no other control.
- **BINDING FROM EZEKIEL ON**, on every book and every generation of this campaign (M7, M8, M9 and successors), and
  it is close-gate item 24: a book does not close while any record implies a provenance it does not have.

