> "if we redo any that are single lane currently. we woudl only need to do it one omre time to hig dual, or do a dual on them to hit tripple."

READING OF THE TERMS (orchestrator's reading, labelled as a reading and correctable by the owner): "tri ban" is
read as TRI-BLIND, "doal" as DUAL, "single band" as SINGLE-LANE. The substance does not depend on the reading:
the owner bans one-lens review, sets dual as the floor, asks that triple be genuinely considered, proposes
revisiting already-closed books after the campaign, and points out that a book already reviewed once needs only
the MISSING lanes rather than a whole new review.

OPERATIONAL READING (orchestrator; correctable by the owner, append-only):

(a) SINGLE-LANE REVIEW IS BANNED, PROSPECTIVELY AND WITHOUT EXCEPTION. No unit group in any book of any
generation may be reviewed by one lens and then treated as reviewed. This is a floor, not a default: it cannot be
waived for an easy book, a short book, a late-campaign book, a budget ceiling or a schedule. A book that cannot
afford two lanes is a book that is not ready to be reviewed. The STANDARD/HARD track distinction of OW-6b governs
coverage, scrutiny and who controls the cycle; it does NOT govern lens count, and no track may drop to one lens.

(b) TWO IS THE FLOOR, THREE IS TO BE CONSIDERED PER BOOK, AND THE CONSIDERATION IS RECORDED. Every book's
strategy states its lens count and the reason, so the choice is visible rather than inherited by habit. An
unrecorded lens count is a form problem at the close gate.

(c) A THIRD LANE ONLY COUNTS IF IT IS DECORRELATED, AND THIS IS THE LOAD-BEARING CLAUSE. The campaign's own
canonical clause already holds that "Anthropic-family agreement is one correlated M8 voice, never independent
confirmation". A third Anthropic-family lane reading the same two witnesses under the same conventions therefore
buys THROUGHPUT, not independence, and a 2-1 split among three correlated lanes is not a majority verdict - it is
one voice plus sampling noise. Reporting such a split as a majority would be an OW-18 breach: it implies
independent confirmation that does not exist. A third lens earns its cost only by breaking a correlation, in
rising order of strength: (i) a different reading ORDER and lens definition - weakest, already used between LF and
OL; (ii) a different EVIDENCE BASE - e.g. a versional/reception lane reading the ancient translations' and the
received tradition's own division points rather than a third pass over the same two witnesses; (iii) a different
MODEL FAMILY, which breaks the prior rather than the evidence; (iv) a HUMAN lens, the only fully out-of-family
lens available, affordable only as a small sample. (ii) and (iii) are the ones worth paying for; (ii) is the
strongest per unit of cost, because it brings evidence the first two lanes never saw.

(d) WHERE A THIRD LENS PAYS, MEASURED ON EZEKIEL RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Across the 123 rows carrying both lanes at
the time of this directive: both lanes challenge 45; one supports and one challenges 35; the lanes propose
different decisions 32; both support with the same decision 11. So two lanes already put 112 of 123 rows (91%)
into conflict or challenge, and the DISCOVERY headroom for a third lens - rows where two lanes agreed and a third
might dissent - is 11 rows. A third lens's real value on a book like this is not discovery but TIE-BREAKING on
the 67 conflict rows, and tie-breaking is exactly the thing a correlated third lane cannot legitimately do. This
is the concrete reason (c) is load-bearing and not a caution.

(e) TARGETED TRI-BLIND IS THE DESIGN THAT ACTUALLY FITS, and it has a leak that must be closed. Running a third
lens only on the conflict classes costs roughly half a full third lane. But a lens selected BY the conflict knows
a conflict exists, which is a blindness leak: it will look for something to find. So a targeted third lane is
given its rows without being told why they were selected, and DECOY rows drawn from the both-support class are
mixed in at a stated rate. Without the decoys the round is not blind and its agreement rate cannot be interpreted.

(f) THE EARLY BOOKS ARE TO BE REVISITED AFTER THE CAMPAIGN, AND THE OW-6c PACKET GAINS A NEW NAMED OPTION. OW-6c
already obliges the Fable controlling agent to present the owner an end-of-campaign re-check decision stating, per
book, which controls were in force. Its alternative list - full re-check, early-books-only, sampled, none - is
hereby EXTENDED with the owner's own cheaper option: LANE TOP-UP, which adds only the missing lanes to a book
already reviewed once instead of re-running the book. The packet must cost and recommend among all five.

(g) TOP-UP ARITHMETIC HOLDS ONLY UNDER RE-DERIVATION, and this is the correction the owner's arithmetic needs.
"One more lane to reach dual" is true if and only if the added lane never sees the existing rows. Blindness is an
INFORMATION BARRIER, NOT A CLOCK: a lane that runs a year later but derives its own boundaries from the witnesses
and the settled conventions, without reading the shipped chunking, is a genuine blind second lane and the
arithmetic is exact. A lane that reviews the EXISTING rows is a different and weaker thing - an audit of lane
one's output, anchored on it - and single-lane plus an audit is NOT dual-blind. Both shapes are legitimate and
they are NEVER to be reported under the same name:

    RETROFIT-REDERIVE - the added lane is blind to the shipped rows and proposes boundaries from the text.
                        Counts toward lens multiplicity. The owner's arithmetic applies.
    RETROFIT-AUDIT    - the added lane reads the shipped rows and critiques them. Does NOT count toward lens
                        multiplicity, and a book carrying it is still recorded as single-lane-plus-audit.

A retrofit record states which shape it was, per book, in its own field. Calling a RETROFIT-AUDIT a second lane
would be precisely the half-truth OW-18 forbids.

(h) REMEDIATE BEFORE YOU RE-REVIEW, unless the owner rules otherwise. Measured from CURRENT_STATE.v1.json
(generated 2026-09-14 from disk, sha256 prefix 2e25bb08): the early-book audits that DID run left 191 open items,
183 of them medium or high, and two of the three remediation dockets (Isaiah LF: 146 items, 0 repairs applied;
Proverbs 38: 33 items, 0 repairs applied) have had no repairs applied at all. Buying a second lens for a book
whose first lens already has 183 unremediated medium/high findings adds findings to a queue that is not being
drained. The OW-6c packet therefore presents remediation status per book ALONGSIDE the re-check options, so the
owner is not choosing between "more review" and "no more review" while the existing findings sit unworked.

(i) NOT RETROACTIVE AS A DEFECT FINDING, AND THE GAP IS STATED RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER. The 25 closed books are
not hereby declared defective; they are declared UNDER-LENSED, which is a different claim, and which one is true
per book is a measurement the OW-6c packet owes rather than an assumption this addendum may make.

STANDING CONSEQUENCE: single-lane review is prohibited campaign-wide; dual-blind is the floor; per-book lens count
and its reason are recorded and gated; a third lane counts only if decorrelated, and a correlated split is never
reported as a majority; OW-6c's option set gains LANE TOP-UP and its packet gains per-book remediation status; and
any retrofit names itself RETROFIT-REDERIVE or RETROFIT-AUDIT. Carried into BIBLE_CHUNKING_METHOD (v5 section 19),
close gate item 25, and every generated resume prompt. Binding on every book and every generation.

