## Addendum 2026-09-15 (E-29, session 910cbe15, during the last Ezekiel primary wave) — WRITE-AT-THE-END: a runtime watchdog turned four nearly-finished reviews into nothing, because the design had each worker write only once, at the end

WHAT HAPPENED. Six primary review executions were in flight. Four of them (`ezek_pr_OL_c20_a1#e1`,
`ezek_pr_LF_c21_a1#e1`, `ezek_pr_OL_c21_a1#e1`, `ezek_pr_LF_c22_a1#e1`) were stopped by the runtime with
"no progress for 600s (stream watchdog did not recover)". Their last surfaced lines show them deep in verification
— one had said it had everything it needed and was about to write. MEASURED immediately afterwards, by exact path:
all four deliverables ABSENT, all six task output files 0 bytes, and a positive control on a landed cluster's
deliverable path PRESENT, which is what makes the absence a real finding rather than a wrong path. The four agents
were then unreachable, so nothing could be recovered by resuming them. **Tier for their findings: UNAVAILABLE.**
Four complete reviews were lost and had to be run again from nothing.

THE ACTUAL DEFECT IS MINE, NOT THE RUNTIME'S. A watchdog killing a long-running worker is an event to design for,
not a surprise. The defect is that each worker wrote its output exactly once, at the very end, so any interruption
before that single write destroyed 100% of the work instead of a delta. The one execution in the wave that
survived intact (`ezek_pr_LF_c20_a1#e1`) did so only because the OW-18 durable-final-message clause had told it to
write its own final message to a file — a control added for provenance reasons, which turned out to be the only
durability control in the wave. That is luck, not design.

THE CURE, STRUCTURAL. (a) WRITE EARLY AND REWRITE: a worker writes its deliverable as soon as it has one finding
per unit, with every outstanding check named in its own uncertainty field, then finishes verifying and rewrites
the same path. Rewriting is expected and is not a defect. (b) THE INSTINCT MUST BE NAMED IN THE BRIEF, because a
careful worker's instinct is to withhold output until it is clean, and that instinct is exactly what a watchdog
converts into total loss; the brief says in terms that a file which exists and discloses its gaps beats a perfect
file that was never written. (c) The re-execution messages were built from the EXACT bytes of the original sent
messages plus a preamble, so nothing about the assignment drifted; the preamble states that the prior execution
produced nothing, which is also why the retry inherits no contamination and remains a genuinely blind first look.
(d) Carried into `BIBLE_CHUNKING_METHOD.v5.md` §10 as a measured warning for every future generation.

MEASURED RESULT OF THE CURE: the first re-execution to return reported writing its deliverable early at one digest
with three open checks disclosed, then rewriting it at the final digest after those checks closed. The design
change works and is observable in the record rather than asserted.

SECOND-ORDER FINDING, and the reason this row matters beyond one wave: **a provenance control turned out to be a
durability control.** OW-18 required the agent to write its own final message so the record would not have to be
transcribed. That requirement is the only reason one of the six reviews survived. Controls justified on honesty
grounds can carry load nobody costed, which is an argument for keeping them when they look redundant.

